  "_comment": "The hosts scripts/compat_check.py asks each app profile about: every ci/images.json image (with its os-release ID and VERSION_ID, so no Docker is needed) plus the distributions the recipes name that have no image in the matrix. `family` is the app's classification (HostRecipeFamily), not the package manager the harness uses. `idLike`: the host's os-release ID_LIKE (read only by readers whose profile has `\"idLike\": \"top-level-allowlist\"`, meshTerm 2.3.2+); measured with `docker run --rm IMAGE cat /etc/os-release` (2026-10-19) or, with no image, from github.com/which-distro/os-release @ 10dfd5bc. scripts/validate.py --declared treats every row with an idLike (classifier ids aside) as an INHERITOR: naming one in a recipe, or no longer naming one, must be declared.",
